			"widgets_values":[
				"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic, vintage film texture with soft halation, a close medium shot frames a man in a well-worn charcoal suit leaning against the aged green-tiled wall of a neon-lit Hong Kong alleyway after rain. A flickering magenta-and-cyan neon sign reading \"重慶夜\" glows in the far background, casting liquid colour washes over the scene. The camera holds a static shot, frame slightly off-kilter as he slowly lifts a half-empty glass of amber whisky. A single drop of condensation slides down the glass. The man with a low, tired, almost murmured baritone (S1) says softly to himself, <d>[Chinese] 那天晚上，我又喝了两杯，以为能把那天晚上的事忘掉。</d> He pauses, then tilts the glass and drains the last sip. [Shot 2] At 00:06.500, the shot transitions to a slow cross-dissolve into a medium-long shot down the length of the same alley, now empty except for the man's silhouette walking away from the camera toward the rain-soaked pavement. The camera performs a gentle, small-amplitude slow Push In as his silhouette grows smaller and the neon reflections stretch and ripple across the wet ground. Steam curls from a distant vent on the right. The man's final words carry over from the previous shot, fading into a soft echo: <scenetrans> continues seamlessly across the cut <scenetrans> <d>[Chinese] 有些人走了，日子照样过。</d> His hands are now empty at his sides. [Shot 3] At 00:11.000, the camera cuts to an extreme close-up of the same condensation drop that ran down the whisky glass in Shot 1, now sliding in slow motion across the polished green tile of the wall. A thin trickle of rainwater merges with it, forming a single curved trail. The neon sign's cyan and magenta hues shiver softly through the droplet. The camera holds a static shot in extreme close-up as the drop reaches a grout line and halts, the last breath of the man's voice echoing faintly off-screen.\n\noverall_soundscape: Low, wet alley ambience with distant street hum and the soft patter of residual rain on the pavement. The whisky glass clinks softly against its coaster as it is lifted, then liquid sloshes gently as the last sip is drained. A distant shutter door clangs once far down the alley, and the faint hiss of steam escapes the vent.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A slow, smoky alto-saxophone solo in a late-night jazz style at a very measured tempo, joined by sparse brushed snare and a single deep upright-bass pedal tone every few bars, volume gradually diminishing into a warm reverb tail that fades out with the final echo of the voice.",
				1152,
				640,
				243
			],
